# {{ projectName }} — Architecture

This project follows **Domain-Driven Design (DDD)** layered architecture with Vapor.

## Layers

### Domain (`Sources/App/Domain/`)
Pure Swift business logic. No Vapor or Fluent dependencies.

- `Entities/` — Fluent models representing core domain objects
- `ValueObjects/` — Immutable typed wrappers for primitive values
- `Aggregates/` — Aggregate roots managing clusters of entities
- `Events/` — Domain events raised by aggregate roots
- `Repositories/` — Repository protocols (interfaces)
- `Services/` — Domain services for cross-entity logic

### Application (`Sources/App/Application/`)
Orchestrates domain objects to fulfill use cases.

- `UseCases/` — One class per use case (Create, GetById, GetAll, Update, Delete)
- `DTOs/` — Input/output types decoupled from domain models

### Infrastructure (`Sources/App/Infrastructure/`)
Implements domain interfaces using Fluent and external services.

- `Repositories/` — Fluent repository implementations
- `Migrations/` — Database schema migrations
- `Seeders/` — Development data seeders

### Presentation (`Sources/App/Presentation/`)
HTTP layer — Vapor controllers, routes, and middleware.

- `Controllers/` — RouteCollection implementations
- `Routes/` — Route registration helpers
- `Middleware/` — Request/response middleware

## Conventions

- Use `PascalCase` for type names
- Suffix repositories with `Repository`, services with `Service`, use cases with `UseCase`
- Register migrations in `configure.swift`
- Register routes via `app.register(collection:)` in `routes.swift`
